Fix: a timed particle emitter loses the particles accrued in the last frame of its duration.

Description
  OGRE 14 changed ParticleEmitter::genConstantEmissionCount so that the particles accrued in a frame
  (mEmissionRate * timeElapsed, kept in mRemainder) are handed out one frame later, and setEnabled() starts an
  emitter with mRemainder = 1 so that its first particle appears at once. When the duration runs out in a frame,
  the emitter is disabled with setEnabled(false), which overwrites mRemainder with 1 and discards everything
  accrued in that last frame. The emitter therefore emits about emission_rate * duration minus up to one frame of
  rate (OGRE 13 handed the accrual out in the same frame and emitted up to one frame more). For short timed
  emitters this is a large share of the burst: "emission_rate 40, duration 0.1" gave 4 instead of 5 particles at
  30 fps, "emission_rate 1000, duration 0.1" gave 101 instead of 133. Emitters without duration, with a negative
  duration (single shot) or with a long duration are not affected visibly.

  The fix returns the whole particles still pending in mRemainder together with the request of the last frame
  before the emitter is disabled. It is the only change; the particle scripts stay as they are.

Affected OGRE file
  OgreMain/src/OgreParticleEmitter.cpp, ParticleEmitter::genConstantEmissionCount, the block
  "if (mDurationRemain <= 0)" (around line 332 of the OGRE 14 tree used here).

Reproduction
  Load any particle system with an emitter "emission_rate 40" and "duration 0.1" (or an equivalent script) and
  count the emitted particles with a fixed 30 fps clock (ParticleSystem::_update(1/30) repeatedly). Without the
  patch the emitter emits 4, with the patch 6 (OGRE 13: 5; the extra one is the first particle that OGRE 14
  emits on enabling). The same holds for every timed emitter whose last frame accrues one or more whole particles.

diff --git a/OgreMain/src/OgreParticleEmitter.cpp b/OgreMain/src/OgreParticleEmitter.cpp
--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreParticleEmitter.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreParticleEmitter.cpp
@@ -331,5 +331,9 @@ namespace Ogre
                 mDurationRemain -= timeElapsed;
                 if (mDurationRemain <= 0) 
                 {
+                    // Hand out the whole particles accrued in the last frame; setEnabled(false) below resets
+                    // mRemainder and would drop them
+                    intRequest += (unsigned short)mRemainder;
                     // Disable, duration is out (takes effect next time)
                     setEnabled(false);
                 }
